# Domains OUTSIDE this subsystem that the ePDG stack needs something from.
# Same split as gnss/, media/, power/, radio/ and nvram/vendor/: a client grant
# belongs beside the other client grants, not in the file that declares the
# type it names.
#
# This file sorts before file.te, which is where every type in this directory is
# declared. That is fine and is the only ordering that is: get_prop() expands to
# `allow`, and checkpolicy resolves an allow rule's operands at link time. Do
# NOT put a `typeattribute` -- or any macro that expands to one, which is every
# net_domain() and hal_*_domain() -- in a file that sorts before file.te.

# libmal_rds.so reads persist.net.wo.debug.* from inside mtkmal -- 26 of them,
# the RAT/RSSI/SNR handover thresholds (persist.net.wo.debug.rdsrat,
# .wifirssih/.wifirssil, .ltersrph/.ltersrpl, .rtp.plrth and the rest). That is
# what this grant is for, and it is the only reason it is load-bearing.
#
# It is NOT justified by the 15 denials an earlier revision of this comment
# cited:
#   avc: denied { read open getattr } for comm="mtkmal"
#        name="u:object_r:mtk_wod_persist_prop:s0" scontext=u:r:mtkmal:s0
# The `name=` there is the property CONTEXT FILE
# /dev/__properties__/u:object_r:mtk_wod_persist_prop:s0 -- one of the 136 files
# in that directory on the handset -- not a property of that type. bionic's
# __system_properties_init/__system_property_foreach opens every context file in
# turn, so a process draws one such denial per type it cannot read whether or
# not it ever reads a property. Proof that those 15 were artefacts: at the time
# they were captured this type labelled only `persist.vendor.wo.` while nothing
# had yet been proven to read it. That prefix IS real -- libmal_rds.so's
# property-name mapper substitutes it for persist.net.wo. whenever
# ro.vendor.md_prop_ver >= 1, which vendor.prop:331 sets -- so mtkmal reads
# persist.vendor.wo.* and this grant is live, not vestigial. See the comment at
# the top of vowifi/property_contexts.
# Read-only: epdg_wod stays the only writer of that namespace.
get_prop(mtkmal, mtk_wod_persist_prop)

# persist.mtk_epdg_support -- the ePDG feature gate, read by mtkmal itself and
# by libmal_epdga.so, the MAL ePDG entity that drives epdg_wod over the two
# init-created sockets (see wod.te). Newly needed because that property is
# labelled mtk_wfc_service_prop as of this change; before, it fell to
# default_prop, which mtkmal could not read either.
get_prop(mtkmal, mtk_wfc_service_prop)

# ImsService (com.mediatek.ims, which runs in the `radio` domain) reads the
# entitlement and operator-list half of the WFC namespace when it evaluates the
# platform WFC switch. Measured, 6 denials in the same boot:
#   avc: denied { read open getattr } for comm="om.mediatek.ims"
#        name="u:object_r:mtk_wfc_service_prop:s0" scontext=u:r:radio:s0
# Read-only. epdg_wod and adb remain the writers.
get_prop(radio, mtk_wfc_service_prop)
